1
00:00:01,420 --> 00:00:04,580
Three frontier models lead rival civilizations

2
00:00:04,580 --> 00:00:06,440
in OpenCivilizationEnv,

3
00:00:06,440 --> 00:00:09,180
and now they talk to each other.

4
00:00:09,180 --> 00:00:10,580
This is the showmatch,

5
00:00:10,580 --> 00:00:14,300
with every message in public and two AI casters.

6
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:15,580
On turn zero,

7
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:17,220
Rome offers friendship,

8
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:19,380
and China adds a warning.

9
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:22,680
Opus spots that each tech is worth four points,

10
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:24,560
and maxes out science.

11
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:27,740
Barbarians loot Kimi's new city seven times,

12
00:00:27,740 --> 00:00:30,450
yet China tells Rome it prospers.

13
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:34,640
Ada: Prosperity is generous, Max.

14
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:36,860
Opus founds four cities first,

15
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:38,730
and signs off as the leader.

16
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:42,230
Ada: But 'whatever the tally' stings a little.

17
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:44,540
Opus wins by eleven points,

18
00:00:44,540 --> 00:00:46,620
and Kimi concedes with grace.

19
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:48,000
In a two-hour game,

20
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,960
they draw a border, cross it, apologize,

21
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:52,940
and team up against Rome.

22
00:00:52,940 --> 00:00:55,560
Each match is one AgentEnv task,

23
00:00:55,560 --> 00:00:58,440
so you choose the agents, models, prompts,

24
00:00:58,440 --> 00:01:00,580
turns, map and casters.

25
00:01:00,580 --> 00:01:02,580
Run it with one command,

26
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:03,380
watch it live,

27
00:01:03,380 --> 00:01:04,880
and keep the recording.

28
00:01:04,880 --> 00:01:07,980
Build your own world with AgentEnv,

29
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:10,370
at agentenvframework.com.
